{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795286979,"nonce":"j+JppAa+jM24LHqac7sPuYbc2c8=","title":"The planes use the models of the asset branch, split into the five parts","message":"\u003e We need to add flares to defend against missiles. We should also pull in game assets from separate branches and keep reading git bug. We also want full screen, \"fuller\" HUD, etc. We have various plane models (players model up planes as they rack up kills) on another branch, but they are not currently destructible. If feasible, deconstruct models into pieces that fit the current model. Current model: destroyed wings or fuselage should be a very quick crash. Add assets (audio, terrain, planes, etc.) as they arrive on different branches. Terrain features need collision detection too.\n\n**Today.** The branch graphic_assets holds one model, a low poly WWI fighter as binary FBX 7.4 with a PNG texture. The engine loads glTF, and not FBX. The model is one piece.\n\n**Outcome.** A build task turns each plane model into a GLB file with five meshes, one for each part of the rules: it scales and turns the model to the size of the rules, and cuts it along the boxes of the parts. The client draws these meshes, so a broken part disappears from the model. A plane changes its model as its pilot scores kills.\n\n**Done when.** A screenshot shows the model in a match, and a second one shows it without a wing.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}